{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Mass.BrunnianTripleExhaustion"],"declarations":5,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.kind_ratio_not_determined_by_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.kind_ratio_not_determined_by_sum","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.lean#L99-L109","doc":"**Why the exhaustion cannot see this.**  Its ratio depends only on the *sum*\nof the counts (`bRatio_depends_only_on_sum`); the kind-dependent ratio does not,\nbecause two carriers with the same total can distribute their crossings over\npairs of different kinds.  So the collapse that makes the exhaustion exhaustive\nis exactly what a kind-dependent weight breaks. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.kindRatio_forced_at_minimal_carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.kindRatio_forced_at_minimal_carrier","kind":"theorem","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.lean#L83-L97","doc":"**The forced kind-ratio for the minimal `³He` carrier.**\n\n`³He` is `ppn`: one `pp` pair and two `pn` pairs.  With the minimal Brunnian\ncounts `mᵢ = 1` and the `pn` weight as the reference, the measured ratio is\nreproduced **iff**\n\n    ρ_pp  =  1 + rMeasured  =  2433859 / 1483044  ≈  1.64112 .\n\nRead RIGHT-TO-LEFT only: this is the number `qou-qqm4`'s derived `z + d_kind` at\nthe `pp` interface must independently produce.  Computing `ρ_pp` from the left is\na one-parameter fit — see the banner above. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.bRatioKind_shifts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.bRatioKind_shifts","kind":"theorem","line":75,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.lean#L75-L81","doc":"**And it is not the same function** — the generalisation has content.  A\nsingle kind whose weight differs moves the ratio by exactly that difference, so\n`bRatioKind` is not constant in `ρ`.  Without this the extension could be\nvacuous. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.bRatioKind_uniform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.bRatioKind_uniform","kind":"theorem","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.lean#L69-L73","doc":"**It is a genuine generalisation**: at uniform weights it is exactly the\nexhaustion's ratio, so nothing here contradicts that file — it extends it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.bRatioKind","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.bRatioKind","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/KindDependentBondBreaksIntegrality.lean#L62-L67","doc":"`b₃/b₂` when the bond weight may depend on the **kind** of pair the interface\njoins.  `ρᵢ` is pair `i`'s weight in units of the reference pair's — and the\nreference is the `pn` pair, because `b₂` is measured on the deuteron, which is\n`pn`.  Setting every `ρᵢ = 1` recovers the uniform case. ","signatureChunk":0}]}